        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.425,
            0.886,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": "We know the line on which D lies. Draw a line through A perpendicular to AB."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.434,
            0.474,
            0.606,
            0.695
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_19_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.711,
            0.884,
            0.755
          ],
          "content": "Now $\\angle \\mathrm { A }$ is divided into two angles. One measures $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ . Check what the other angle is."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.245,
            0.768,
            0.8,
            0.791
          ],
          "content": "There are at least two ways of finding the point D —"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.794,
            0.884,
            0.837
          ],
          "content": "One uses the fact that all the angles of a rectangle are right angles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.841,
            0.794,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": "• The other uses the fact that opposite sides are equal."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.082,
